---
/** D8: AID compared with spec-driven development. Drawing and table carry the same statements. */
import Diagram from '../Diagram.astro';
const id = 'aid-vs-sdd';
const arrow = `url(#dg-${id}-arrow)`;
---
<Diagram id={id} width={400} height={480}
  title="AID compared with spec-driven development"
  desc="Spec-driven development starts with a spec, and specifications drive code generation. AID's decision record describes spec-driven development as re-specifying from scratch on change. AID starts with knowledge: /aid-discover builds the Knowledge Base for an existing project. Then come Describe, Define, Specify, Plan, Detail and Execute, with your approval at each phase of the full path. A change goes back through the phases that need it. AID also includes a spec-and-build layer."
  caption="Spec-driven development and AID, side by side.">
  <text class="dg-label" x="8" y="28">Spec-driven<tspan x="8" dy="1.25em">development</tspan></text>
  <rect class="dg-node" x="8" y="72" width="160" height="48" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="88" y="91" text-anchor="middle">Start with<tspan x="88" dy="1.25em">a spec</tspan></text>
  <path class="dg-edge" d="M88 120 V152" marker-end={arrow} />
  <rect class="dg-node" x="8" y="152" width="160" height="64" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="88" y="169" text-anchor="middle">Specifications<tspan x="88" dy="1.25em">drive code</tspan><tspan x="88" dy="1.25em">generation</tspan></text>
  <path class="dg-edge" d="M88 216 V248" marker-end={arrow} />
  <rect class="dg-node" x="8" y="248" width="160" height="64" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="88" y="265" text-anchor="middle">A change means<tspan x="88" dy="1.25em">re-specifying</tspan><tspan x="88" dy="1.25em">from scratch</tspan></text>
  <text class="dg-note" x="88" y="332" text-anchor="middle">(as AID's decision<tspan x="88" dy="1.25em">record describes it)</tspan></text>
  <path class="dg-edge dg-optional" d="M168 280 H176 V96 H168" marker-end={arrow} />

  <text class="dg-label" x="184" y="28">AID (AI Integrated<tspan x="184" dy="1.25em">Development)</tspan></text>
  <rect class="dg-node dg-accent" x="184" y="72" width="208" height="80" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="288" y="87" text-anchor="middle">Knowledge first:<tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">/aid-discover builds</tspan><tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">the Knowledge Base</tspan><tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">(existing project)</tspan></text>
  <path class="dg-edge" d="M288 152 V184" marker-end={arrow} />
  <rect class="dg-node" x="184" y="184" width="208" height="64" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="288" y="201" text-anchor="middle">Describe, Define,<tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">Specify, Plan,</tspan><tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">Detail, Execute</tspan></text>
  <path class="dg-edge" d="M288 248 V280" marker-end={arrow} />
  <rect class="dg-node" x="184" y="280" width="208" height="48" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="288" y="299" text-anchor="middle">You approve each<tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">phase (full path)</tspan></text>
  <path class="dg-edge" d="M288 328 V360" marker-end={arrow} />
  <rect class="dg-node" x="184" y="360" width="208" height="64" rx="6" />
  <text class="dg-label" x="288" y="377" text-anchor="middle">A change goes back<tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">through the phases</tspan><tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">that need it</tspan></text>
  <text class="dg-note" x="288" y="448" text-anchor="middle">Includes a spec-and-build<tspan x="288" dy="1.25em">layer</tspan></text>

  <table slot="text">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Topic</th><th scope="col">Spec-driven development</th><th scope="col">AID (AI Integrated Development)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Where it starts</th><td>with a spec</td><td>with knowledge: <code>/aid-discover</code> builds the Knowledge Base for an existing project</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">How the work proceeds</th><td>specifications drive code generation</td><td>Describe, Define, Specify, Plan, Detail and Execute, with your approval at each phase of the full path; AID also includes a spec-and-build layer</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">When something changes</th><td>re-specifying from scratch, as AID's decision record describes spec-driven development</td><td>the work goes back through the phases that need it</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</Diagram>
